  "result": "Fixed in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. The cause was that Python's `shlex` treats `#` as a comment character by default. It silently dropped everything from a `#` onward, so completion saw a truncated argument list. I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` to turn that off.\n\n`split_arg_string('ex a#b #c')` now returns `['ex', 'a#b', '#c']`, and `tests/test_shell_completion.py` passes (58 tests). I didn't add a regression test for this one either.",
